Author: zlink-systems <zlink@zlink.systems>
Date:   Sun Nov 8 06:39:35 2026 +0900

    perf(dotnet): hand the receive role to an unstarted application reservation (#1639)
    
    At the end of a receive pass, the process execution pool now gives the
    receiving worker an application reservation that its worker has not started,
    and assigns the donor worker the next receive pass (spec 08 section 4.4).
    A NodeRequest that arrives on an idle pool then runs its handler on the
    worker that received it, without a wake and a thread switch. If no unstarted
    reservation exists, the pool is stopping, or the source is closing, the
    receiver keeps its role. The receive role moves only under the existing
    gate, and at most one worker receives at a time.
    
    MeshReceiveHandoffTests asserted that the receive thread stays the same
    across passes. Spec 08 section 4.4 ties the receive role to no thread, so
    those assertions now check that the blocked handler is not the receiver.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01D9jfevecSH9qJxjtX358f4

